# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A call crosses a blank line"

# TiddlyWiki carries a call across a blank line and builds it — measured, one blank line or many,
# inline and block alike. So no blank-line bound belongs on a call's end: cutting there reads the
# closer as whatever the line looks like standing alone, and a reader loses a construct the host
# keeps. Here the closer would read as a blockquote.
#
# corpus/carrier-ledger.txt rules the runaway this leaves standing, where a value's closing quote
# reaches nowhere in the source and the region meets nothing to close on.

* <<myCall

  >>
#  ^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.list.unnumbered.unordered.ul.li.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.procedurecallinline.end.tiddlywiki5

<<myCall

>>
#^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallblock.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.procedurecallblock.end.tiddlywiki5
